I bought the Metro Redux Bundle, played and finished both games back-to-back in one or two weeks time.
I played both games in Survival Hardcore, and I got good endings for both.
I'm really glad I played Metro 2033 Redux right before this one, as it set up the characters and the story (which is actually really important IMO, I would not have understood most of what's going on in Last Light otherwise). Also, I'm glad that the intrigue that Metro 2033 brought me, made me play Last Light afterwards, because I greatly enjoyed LL.
To me, this game feels like an advancement in many ways, compared to the previous title.
Pros:
- Levels are beautifully crafted, feel very rich and vibrant, and are very diverse throughout the game (much more so than Metro2033);
- Atmosphere is even better than the previous game, with a few spider levels that felt properly spooky;
- Gunplay is also improved, with good controls for most guns (I did not try them all out);
- Storyline is awesome, I really loved the companions that come with you along the way in certain parts of the story, One in particular (although I won't say which, that might be a spoiler);
- Once again, great companions and characters in this game, I can't overstate that.
Cons:
- I read about the morality system in this game being very strict, which led to me having to reload checkpoints MANY times, which was extremely infuriating and frustrating, all because I wanted the good ending. I don't feel like killing the nazis and Reds, who both torture♥♥♥♥♥♥pillage wherever they please, should be regarded as a bad thing, so getting a moral point for not killing any of them in a level feels very stupid (killing them would save others, I'm sure);
- The ending is not as unique and interesting as the previous game's ending, it feels much more generic here.
Overall, I was extremely pleased with this game, and it will stay in my list of favorite games of all time.
I can't exactly describe why I like this game so much more than 2033, even though I played that one first.
I'm giving this title an 8.5/10, I could give it more but then a "10" would become less meaningful..

